title: The Central Committee
subtitle: Rákosi comes to Berlin to settle accounts.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1921 and month = 2 and e21_cc_done = 0 and e21_levi_leads = 1 and levi_in_party = 1 and congress = 0 and crisis = 0
max-visits: 1
priority: 10
on-arrival: {!
Q.e21_cc_done = 1;
Q.comintern_rep = 'Mátyás Rákosi';
// the year so far decides how the members of the committee lean before anyone speaks
var p = 35;
p += 3 * ((Q.history_luxemburgist || 0) - (Q.history_offensive || 0));
p += (Q.independence - 50) / 2;
p += (Q.luxemburgist_satisfaction - Q.offensive_satisfaction) / 4;
if (Q.e21_livorno == 1) { p += 10; }
if (Q.open_letter == 1) { p += 5; }
if (Q.luxemburg_alive == 1) { p += 25; }
p += (Q.ecci_radek - 50) / 5;
Q.e21_cc_win_chance = Math.round(Math.max(10, Math.min(85, p)));
Q.e21_cc_odds = (Q.e21_cc_win_chance < 30) ? 'poor' : ((Q.e21_cc_win_chance < 55) ? 'uncertain' : 'good');
// a fraction of the committee that moves before the debate: positive for Levi
Q.e21_cc_tilt = (Q.e21_cc_win_chance - 45) / 100;
!}

= The Central Committee

From 22 to 24 February the Central Committee meets in Berlin. Rákosi has come straight from Livorno. He puts a resolution approving the Italian split, and everyone understands that it is a vote on Levi.

[? if e21_livorno = 1 : Levi's articles defending Serrati are quoted against him, line by line. ?][? if e21_livorno = 3 : The Rote Fahne has already endorsed the split, over Levi's silence. He is fighting on ground he gave up. ?]

[? if luxemburg_alive = 1 : Rosa Luxemburg speaks before the vote. She says that a party which takes its orders on Italy from a Hungarian it has never elected will soon take its orders on Germany the same way. ?][? if luxemburg_alive = 0 : Clara Zetkin speaks for Levi. Thalheimer, Frölich and the Berlin delegates speak for Rákosi. ?] Levi has said that if the resolution passes, he will resign the chair, and Zetkin, Däumig, Adolph Hoffmann and Otto Brass will go with him.

Heinrich Brandler has a resolution of his own in his pocket: Livorno approved in principle, Levi kept in the chair. He will table it if the Zentrale asks him to.

- @fight: Fight the vote, and win it.
- @compromise: Ask Brandler to table his compromise.
- @resign: Let Levi resign in protest.
- @accept: Accept Moscow's verdict to keep Levi in the chair.
- @rakosi: Back Rákosi, and bring in a new Zentrale.

@fight
subtitle: The Spartacist line. Levi counts the votes: his chances look [+ e21_cc_odds +]. If we lose, we lose the chair.
on-arrival: {!
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 3;
Q.e21_cc_mode = 1;
RG.congressStart({
    id: 'cc21',
    name: 'The Central Committee',
    stake: 'Rákosi\'s resolution on Livorno, and Levi\'s chair',
    sessions: 2,
    positions: ['luxemburgist', 'offensive'],
    backing: 'luxemburgist',
    kind: 'motion',
    mandates: 'zentrale',
    delegates: 51,
    ownClose: true
});
// Thalheimer and much of the Right side with Rákosi against Levi
RG.congress.swayTo('offensive', 0.07);
if (Q.e21_cc_tilt > 0) { RG.congress.sway(Q.e21_cc_tilt * 0.5); } else { RG.congress.lose(-Q.e21_cc_tilt * 0.6); }
RG.congress.bitter(3);
RG.ecci('zinoviev', -3);
!}

The Zentrale will fight. Levi spends the evening before the session with a list of the fifty-one members of the committee and a pencil. By midnight there are ticks, crosses and too many question marks.

@compromise
subtitle: The Right's way. Levi stays if Brandler's motion carries, and Moscow gets half of what it asked. Neither Levi nor Rákosi will thank us.
on-arrival: {!
Q.lean_unionist += 2;
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 1;
Q.e21_cc_mode = 2;
RG.congressStart({
    id: 'cc21',
    name: 'The Central Committee',
    stake: 'Brandler\'s compromise on Livorno, and Levi\'s chair',
    sessions: 2,
    positions: ['unionist', 'offensive'],
    backing: 'unionist',
    kind: 'motion',
    mandates: 'zentrale',
    delegates: 51,
    ownClose: true
});
if (Q.e21_cc_tilt > 0) { RG.congress.sway(Q.e21_cc_tilt * 0.5); } else { RG.congress.lose(-Q.e21_cc_tilt * 0.4); }
RG.ecci('radek', 3);
!}

Brandler tables his resolution. Levi withdraws his own and tells his friends to vote for Brandler's, without enthusiasm. Rákosi says that a compromise with centrism is centrism.

@resign
subtitle: What history did. Brandler and Stoecker take over, and the theory of the offensive comes with them.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e21_levi_resigned = 1;
Q.e21_levi_leads = 0;
Q.e21_lux_leads = 0;
Q.leading_faction = 'offensive';
Q.junior_faction = 'unionist';
Q.luxemburgist_satisfaction -= 8;
Q.offensive_satisfaction += 12;
Q.independence -= 5;
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 1;
Q.lean_offensive += 1;
RG.setRole('levi', 'Reichstag deputy');
RG.setRole('brandler', 'Chairman of the Zentrale');
RG.comply(100);
RG.ecci('zinoviev', 6);
RG.ecci('lenin', -3);
RG.news('Levi and Zetkin resign from the Zentrale', 3);
RG.ledger('Paul Levi resigned the chair after the Central Committee approved Livorno.', 'e21_levi_resigned');
!}

Rákosi's resolution passes, 28 votes to 23. Levi, Zetkin, Däumig, Hoffmann and Brass resign from the Zentrale. They mean it as a warning. Rákosi takes it as a victory. Heinrich Brandler and Walter Stoecker take the chair, and the new Zentrale, with Thalheimer and Paul Frölich at its side, begins to talk about the offensive.

@accept
subtitle: [? if lock_moscow_orders = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] Levi stays, humbled. The Right approves. The Spartacists feel betrayed by their own leader.
choose-if: lock_moscow_orders < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids taking orders from Moscow.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_moscow_orders == 1) {
    Q.unity -= 10;
    Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10;
}
Q.independence -= 8;
Q.luxemburgist_satisfaction -= 10;
Q.unionist_satisfaction += 8;
Q.offensive_satisfaction -= 2;
Q.unity += 5;
Q.junior_faction = 'unionist';
Q.lean_unionist += 2;
RG.comply(100);
RG.ecci('radek', 4);
RG.news('Levi bows to Moscow: the Central Committee approves Livorno', 3);
!}

Levi swallows the resolution. He votes for it himself, and keeps the chair. Zetkin does not speak to him for a week. Rákosi reports to Moscow that the German leadership can be bent.

@rakosi
subtitle: [? if lock_moscow_orders = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] The Left's line. Levi goes, and the Left takes seats in the new Zentrale.
choose-if: lock_moscow_orders < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids taking orders from Moscow.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_moscow_orders == 1) {
    Q.unity -= 10;
}
Q.e21_levi_resigned = 1;
Q.e21_levi_leads = 0;
Q.e21_lux_leads = 0;
Q.leading_faction = 'offensive';
Q.junior_faction = 'unionist';
Q.independence -= 10;
Q.luxemburgist_satisfaction -= 15;
Q.offensive_satisfaction += 15;
Q.lean_offensive += 3;
Q.lean_luxemburgist -= 2;
RG.setRole('levi', 'Reichstag deputy');
RG.setRole('brandler', 'Chairman of the Zentrale');
RG.setRole('fischer', 'Berlin organiser; member of the Zentrale');
RG.comply(100);
RG.ecci('zinoviev', 10);
RG.ecci('bukharin', 6);
RG.ecci('lenin', -5);
RG.news('The Zentrale backs Rákosi: Levi and his friends resign', 3);
RG.ledger('The Zentrale itself turned on Levi in February 1921.', 'e21_cc_rakosi');
!}

The Zentrale itself backs Rákosi. The resolution passes by a wide margin, and Levi and his friends resign. Brandler and Stoecker take the chair. Ruth Fischer's Berlin delegates are given a voice in the new Zentrale, and they intend to use it.
